# Release consumer checks must use explicit status, not assert
id:                     E7004-draft-2301_80739235
trigger_tool:           conan-create|cmake|clang
phase:                  package-validation|consumer-test
error_signature:        "assert.*NDEBUG|Release.*assert|consumer.*PASS.*without.*check"
severity:               3
category:               consumer-validation|release-build
match_keywords:         NDEBUG assertion removal, explicit consumer failure status, release test validation
root_cause:             The C and C++ assert macros are removed when NDEBUG is defined, so a consumer test that only uses assert can print PASS after an incorrect result in the default Release configuration.
affected_scope:         Conan test_package consumers and cross-built validation binaries compiled with Release or NDEBUG.
verification_cmd:       Build the consumer in Release, inspect the binary path, and exercise a deliberate mismatch to require a non-zero exit; then run the real consumer and require the expected PASS output.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           explicit-status-check
rec_description:        Replace assertion-only validation with an explicit condition that reports the mismatch and returns non-zero before any PASS marker.
rec_command:            "if (actual != expected) { report failure; return 1; }"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               test_package
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      dual-configuration-consumer
fallback_description:   If an assertion is retained for diagnostics, pair it with an explicit status check that remains active under NDEBUG.
fallback_command:       "compile Release/NDEBUG and require a non-zero mismatch result"
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          consumer-validation
forbid_1_pattern:       "assert.*PASS|assert.*consumer.*only"
forbid_1_reason:        Release removes the assertion expression and can turn a failed semantic check into a false pass.
forbid_1_consequence:   Package validation claims correctness without checking the produced values.
principles:             P007, P015
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
doc_file:               drafts/E7004-draft-2301_80739235.md
last_updated:           2026-09-07
source_event:           onetbb/2023.1.0 platform AI Review P3 on test_package/test_onetbb.cpp
